Aqua Operator – Short Development Guide
======================================

Prereqs
- Go toolchain, Docker (for images), access to a Kubernetes/OLM cluster if you deploy.
- Tools are auto-downloaded by Makefile targets (controller-gen, kustomize, yq, opm).

Core workflow
- Edit API types under `apis/operator/v1alpha1`. Add fields with JSON tags.
- Run codegen and CRDs:
  - `make generate`          # updates zz_generated.deepcopy.go
  - `make manifests`         # regenerates CRDs under config/crd/bases
- Implement controllers/helpers under `controllers/...` to use new spec fields.
- Build/test locally: `make build` (or `make test`).
- Generate bundle for OLM: `make bundle VERSION=x.y.z`
  - Build/push bundle image: `make bundle-build BUNDLE_IMG=... && make bundle-push BUNDLE_IMG=...`

Example: adding the Trivy component (what we did)
- API/CRDs:
  - Added AquaTrivy CRD files under `config/crd/bases` (split per CRD).
  - Updated CSV owned/internal-objects to list the CRDs.
- Controller/Helper:
  - `controllers/aquasecurity/aquatrivy/aquatrivy_controller.go` ensures all Trivy resources exist (RBAC, ConfigMaps, Secrets, Service, Deployment).
  - `controllers/aquasecurity/aquatrivy/aquaTrivyHelper.go` builds those resources:
    - Operator config via `trivy-operator-config` (mounted with envFrom on the trivy-operator pod).
    - Operator settings and scanner settings ConfigMaps.
    - Deployment with writable emptyDir mounts for /tmp and /var/trivyoperator, and envFrom for the ConfigMap.
  - Removed unused Trivy CRDs and their RBAC entries when no longer needed.
- Bundle:
  - Regenerated with `make bundle` after changes so OLM ships the updated CSV/CRDs.

Example: adding env support to AquaScanner (mirrors AquaServer)
- Added `Envs []corev1.EnvVar \`json:"env,omitempty"\`` to `apis/operator/v1alpha1/aquascanner_types.go`.
- Regenerated code/CRDs: `make generate && make manifests`.
- In `controllers/operator/aquascanner/aquaScannerHelper.go`, appended `spec.env` into the scanner container’s Env list.
- After bundle rebuild, users can set envs in the AquaScanner CR:
  ```
  spec:
    env:
      - name: MY_FLAG
        value: "true"
  ```

Generated files
- Do not hand-edit `zz_generated.deepcopy.go` or CRDs in `config/crd/bases`; always rerun `make generate` / `make manifests`.

Common Make targets
- `make generate`    — deepcopy code
- `make manifests`   — CRDs
- `make build`       — manager binary
- `make bundle`      — OLM bundle (uses kustomize/yq/operator-sdk)
- `make bundle-build` / `make bundle-push` — bundle image
- `make catalog-build` / `make catalog-push` — catalog image (optional)

Deployment (manual, non-OLM)
- `make install` to apply CRDs, `make deploy` to deploy controller into cluster.
- `make undeploy` / `make uninstall` to remove.

Tips
- Keep API, controller, helper, and CRD in sync; regenerate after API changes.
- When adding a new component/CRD, update the CSV owned/internal-objects before bundling.
- Prefer envFrom for ConfigMap-driven settings; avoid hard-coding generated settings.

Directory structure (key paths)
- `apis/operator/v1alpha1/`     — CRD types (spec/status) for operator resources.
- `controllers/`                — Reconcilers and helpers for each CR/feature.
- `config/crd/bases/`           — Generated CRDs (from make manifests).
- `config/manifests/`           — Kustomize bases/overlays used to render the bundle/manager.
- `bundle/`                     — OLM bundle output (CSV + CRDs) after make bundle.
- `Makefile`                    — Entrypoint for generate/manifests/build/bundle commands.
- `hack/boilerplate.go.txt`     — Header used during codegen.

